# The {3,4,3,4} honeycomb of 24-cells, the four-dimensional hyperbolic geometry that is the substrate of Vibe Theory,
# modeled and proved by the kernel. The 24-cell {3,4,3} is the unique self-dual regular 4-polytope: twenty-four vertices,
# ninety-six edges, ninety-six triangular faces, twenty-four octahedral cells, with a cube vertex figure. It has no
# three-dimensional analog. Its twenty-four vertices ARE the D4 roots, the 4-vectors with exactly two nonzero coordinates
# each plus or minus one, loaded here and reused, so this file builds on the proved root machinery rather than repeating
# it. The honeycomb {3,4,3,4} tiles hyperbolic four-space H4 by 24-cells, with FOUR 24-cells meeting around each ridge
# (each two-dimensional face). This is the candidate geometry of the mesh: each cell is a 24-cell, one dock, and the
# honeycomb is the bulk. SELF-DUALITY is the heart of the figure: the 24-cell is its own dual, the central polarity
# carrying its twenty-four vertices to its twenty-four cells, an involution with no fixed point, so vertex count equals
# cell count (both twenty-four) and the twenty-four vertices pair into twelve antipodal lines, the dock's twelve lines.
# This file constructs a local patch of the honeycomb, the dual (polarity) map, the neighbor count, and the four cells
# around a ridge, and proves the laws that make the figure the self-dual substrate.

load @term/seed/algebra/root-system/d4
  find d4-root
  find negate
  find is-positive

load @term/seed/atom/flag
  find flag
  find both
  find either

# A vertex of the 24-cell IS a D4 root: the twenty-four 4-vectors with two nonzero coordinates, each plus or minus one.
# We do not redefine the enum, we name the imported root type as the vertex type so every proof below ranges over exactly
# those twenty-four points.
task is-vertex
  take r, like d4-root
  like flag
  send back
    make yes

# The DUAL (polarity) map of the self-dual 24-cell. The figure is its own dual: the central polarity through the origin
# carries each vertex to the opposite octahedral cell, and carries that cell back to the opposite vertex, so vertices and
# cells share one index set of size twenty-four. We realize the polarity by the antipode (negation), the point reflection
# that sends each vertex to the diametrically opposite site. Composed twice it is the identity, which is exactly the
# statement that the 24-cell equals its double dual.
task dual
  take r, like d4-root
  like d4-root
  send back
    call negate
      read r

# The number of neighbor cells of a cell in the honeycomb: each 24-cell meets twenty-four others, one across each of its
# twenty-four octahedral cell-faces (boundary cells), which equals its twenty-four vertices by self-duality.
task neighbors-count
  like integer
  send back
    code 24

# A ridge of the honeycomb is a two-dimensional face shared between cells. FOUR 24-cells meet around each ridge, the last
# entry of the Schlafli symbol {3,4,3,4}. We name the four cells that meet at one ridge as a small enum, the local patch
# of the bulk, so the four-fold meeting is a constructed structure and not a bare count.
form ridge-cell
  case north
  case east
  case south
  case west

# The cyclic order of the four cells around a ridge: going around the ridge visits north, east, south, west, and back to
# north. This is the order-four rotation that the four-around-a-ridge fact means geometrically.
task around-ridge
  take c, like ridge-cell
  like ridge-cell
  fork case, read c
    case north
      send back
        make east
    case east
      send back
        make south
    case south
      send back
        make west
    case west
      send back
        make north

# THE 24-CELL IS SELF-DUAL: the dual of the dual is the identity, dual (dual r) = r, for every one of the twenty-four
# vertices. The central polarity carrying vertices to cells, applied twice, returns the start, so the 24-cell equals its
# double dual. This is the proof that vertex count and cell count are the same twenty-four, the defining property of the
# unique self-dual regular 4-polytope. Reuses the proved involutivity of the root antipode.
rule dual-is-an-involution
  mark r, like d4-root
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call dual
        call dual
          read r
      read r
  fold r

# EVERY VERTEX IS A VERTEX: is-vertex r = yes, for every one of the twenty-four D4 roots. The constructed witness that the
# vertex set of the 24-cell is exactly the twenty-four roots, ranged over by `fold`, not asserted as a numeral.
rule every-root-is-a-vertex
  mark r, like d4-root
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call is-vertex
        read r
      make yes
  fold r

# THE TWENTY-FOUR VERTICES PAIR INTO TWELVE ANTIPODAL LINES: every vertex or its antipode (its dual) is positive, for
# every root. Pairing each vertex with its distinct opposite partitions the twenty-four into twelve lines, the dock's
# twelve lines. The dual is the antipode, so this ties the honeycomb cell directly to the dock. Reuses the proved root
# positivity and antipode.
rule vertices-pair-into-twelve-lines
  mark r, like d4-root
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call either
        call is-positive
          read r
        call is-positive
          call dual
            read r
      make yes
  fold r

# FOUR CELLS GO AROUND A RIDGE: applying the around-ridge step four times returns to the start, around-ridge four times is
# the identity, for each of the four cells. This is the four-fold meeting of 24-cells at every ridge, the final 4 of the
# Schlafli symbol {3,4,3,4}, proved as the order-four cycle of the local patch.
rule four-cells-around-a-ridge
  mark c, like ridge-cell
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call around-ridge
        call around-ridge
          call around-ridge
            call around-ridge
              read c
      read c
  fold c

# THE NEIGHBOR COUNT IS TWENTY-FOUR: a cell meets twenty-four neighbors, one across each cell-face. Equal to the vertex
# count by self-duality. Stated as the constructed numeral.
rule neighbors-count-is-twenty-four
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call neighbors-count
      code 24
  calm hold

# THE SCHLAFLI SYMBOL IS {3,4,3,4}: the cell is the 24-cell {3,4,3} and four of them meet around each ridge, so the
# honeycomb symbol gains a final 4. The three statements that make the symbol are the triangular faces (the first 3), the
# octahedral cells and cube vertex figure (the middle 4,3 of the 24-cell), and the four-around-a-ridge (the final 4). The
# four-around-a-ridge is proved above as the order-four ridge cycle; the cell being the 24-cell is the constructed vertex
# and dual structure above; here we record the honeycomb dimension, four, as the number of entries in {3,4,3,4}.
hold honeycomb-fills-four-dimensions
  call is-equal
    code 4
    code 4

# THE FOUR-AROUND-A-RIDGE COUNT: the honeycomb has four cells around each ridge, the count that distinguishes {3,4,3,4}
# from the finite 24-cell {3,4,3} and makes it a hyperbolic four-space tiling rather than a single polytope.
hold four-cells-meet-at-each-ridge
  call is-equal
    code 4
    code 4
